    "fileId": 540,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Anal squamous cell carcinoma</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Arising from overlying high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion with haphazard stromal invasion.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "Rondell P. Graham",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/72/540.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/72/thumb_540.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32111,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 72,
    "fileId": 541,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Anal squamous cell carcinoma</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>p16 immunohistochemistry is strongly and diffusely positive in the invasive carcinoma and overlying high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion, characteristic of an HPV-positive carcinoma.</p>",
    "source": "Rondell P. Graham",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/72/541.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/72/thumb_541.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32112,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 72,
    "fileId": 542,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Anal squamous cell carcinoma</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>HPV&nbsp;E6/E7&nbsp;mRNA in situ hybridization is positive, indicating transcriptionally active high-risk HPV in the tumour cells of the squamous cell carcinoma.</p>",
    "source": "Rondell P. Graham",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/72/542.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/72/thumb_542.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32115,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 72,
    "fileId": 545,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Anal squamous cell carcinoma (SCC)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>The neoplasm shows a peripheral palisade of darker-staining cells within the invasive trabecula; this imparts a basaloid appearance to the SCC. Focal keratinization is noted.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "Rondell P. Graham",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/72/545.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/72/thumb_545.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32117,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 72,
    "fileId": 547,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Anal squamous cell carcinoma (SCC)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Hyaline material encircles and percolates into tumour trabecula, giving rise to an adenoid cystic&ndash;like appearance. This histological finding may be seen admixed with areas of conventional-looking SCC.</p>",
    "source": "Rondell P. Graham",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/72/547.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/72/thumb_547.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32134,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 72,
    "fileId": 584,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Anal squamous cell carcinoma (SCC)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Anal SCC may display a morphological pattern reminiscent of urothelial carcinoma. In this field, overt squamous differentiation is inapparent, and the tumour cells have a transitional-like appearance.</p>",
    "source": "Rondell P. Graham",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/72/584.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/72/thumb_584.jpg"
  },
